//! x86-64 machine-code generation for the supported subset.
//!
//! Type-aware. Every expression evaluates into `RAX`; integers live in `EAX`
//! (32-bit), pointers / 8-byte values in the full `RAX`. An lvalue path
//! (`gen_addr`) yields an address so `&`, `*`, `[]`, assignment and
//! `++`/`--` work uniformly. Pointer arithmetic scales by the pointee size;
//! loads/stores are sized (with sign/zero extension) by the static type.
//!
//! Globals live in a writable `.data` image the linker places; references use
//! RIP-relative addressing resolved as `RipRef::Data`. Naive (no register
//! allocation) but correct and extensible.
//!
//! ## Module organisation (S1a split)
//!
//! As of S1a (May-26 plan §4) this file is the codegen orchestrator and
//! holds the per-function `Gen` state object + its lowest-level primitives.
//! ABI-specific encoding constants and the Win64 aggregate classifier
//! live in [`abi`]; further submodules (cpp / decl / stmt / expr) will
//! land in subsequent extractions. Already-extracted EH machinery lives
//! in [`crate::eh`].

pub(crate) mod abi;
pub(crate) mod cpp;
pub(crate) mod decl;
pub mod encoder;
pub(crate) mod expr;
pub(crate) mod object;
pub(crate) mod statics;
pub(crate) mod stmt;
pub mod target;
pub(crate) mod template;

