                // definition — `::operator new[](sz)` etc. (ClassLib's
                // allocators forward to these). mdbcc has no runtime to link
                // them against; provide them intrinsically as HeapAlloc /
                // HeapFree. A user-defined global operator (registered under
                // the bare name in funcs/overloads) takes the normal path; a
                // class member operator is registered under `Tag::operator …`,
                // so this never shadows one.
                // Only the STANDARD single-argument global forms are the
                // intrinsic (size_t for new, void* for delete). Multi-argument
                // forms — placement `operator new(size_t, void*)`, allocator
                // `operator new[](size_t, Alloc&)` — are user/friend-defined and
                // fall through to normal overload resolution. mdbcc ships no
                // runtime, so the 1-arg global allocators are always intrinsic.
                if args.len() == 1
                    && matches!(
                        name.as_str(),
                        "operator new" | "operator new[]" | "operator delete" | "operator delete[]"
                    )
                {
                    return self.gen_global_alloc_op(name, args);
                }
